    "category": "Normal Distribution",
    "weightBadge": "S1",
    "topics": [
      "\\(X\\sim N(\\mu,\\sigma^2)\\)",
      "Standardising \\(Z=\\tfrac{X-\\mu}{\\sigma}\\)",
      "Tables &amp; symmetry",
      "Finding \\(\\mu\\) or \\(\\sigma\\)"
    ]
  },
  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "topicGrid",
        "items": [
          {
            "title": "The Normal Curve",
            "body": "Bell-shaped, symmetric about mean \\(\\mu\\). \\(X\\sim N(\\mu,\\sigma^2)\\). Approximately 68%/95%/99.7% within 1/2/3 standard deviations."
          },
          {
            "title": "Standardising",
            "body": "\\(Z=\\dfrac{X-\\mu}{\\sigma}\\sim N(0,1)\\). Use \\(Z\\)-tables (standard normal) to find probabilities."
          },
          {
            "title": "Finding Probabilities",
            "body": "\\(P(X&lt;a)=\\Phi\\!\\left(\\dfrac{a-\\mu}{\\sigma}\\right)\\). Use symmetry: \\(P(Z&lt;-z)=1-P(Z&lt;z)\\)."
          },
          {
            "title": "Inverse Normal",
            "body": "Given probability, find the value. \\(P(X&lt;a)=p\\Rightarrow a=\\mu+z\\sigma\\) where \\(z=\\Phi^{-1}(p)\\)."
          },
          {
            "title": "Finding μ or σ",
            "body": "Set up two equations from given probabilities, solve simultaneously for unknown parameters."
          },
          {
            "title": "Normal Approximation",
            "body": "To Binomial \\(B(n,p)\\): if \\(n\\) large, \\(np&gt;5\\), \\(n(1-p)&gt;5\\): use \\(N(np,np(1-p))\\) with continuity correction \\(\\pm0.5\\)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Normal Distribution — Reference",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "If \\(X\\sim N(\\mu,\\sigma^2)\\): standardise with \\(Z=\\dfrac{X-\\mu}{\\sigma}\\) where \\(Z\\sim N(0,1)\\). Use tables (or calculator) for \\(\\Phi(z)=P(Z\\leq z)\\). Key symmetry: \\(P(Z\\leq -z)=1-P(Z\\leq z)\\). For <strong>inverse normal</strong>: given a probability, find the corresponding \\(x\\) value using \\(x=\\mu+z\\sigma\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Standardise",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\(Z=\\dfrac{X-\\mu}{\\sigma}\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Symmetry",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\(P(Z\\leq-z)=1-\\Phi(z)\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Inverse normal",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\(x=\\mu+z\\sigma\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Normal approx to B",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "Use when \\(n\\) large, \\(p\\approx0.5\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Finding a probability",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>\\(X\\sim N(50,16)\\) so \\(\\sigma=4\\). Find \\(P(44\\leq X\\leq58)\\).</p>\\[P\\!\\left(\\frac{44-50}{4}\\leq Z\\leq\\frac{58-50}{4}\\right)=P(-1.5\\leq Z\\leq 2)=\\Phi(2)-\\Phi(-1.5).\\]\\[=0.9772-(1-0.9332)=0.9772-0.0668=0.9104.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Finding \\(\\mu\\)",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>\\(X\\sim N(\\mu,25)\\). Given \\(P(X&gt;43)=0.2119\\), find \\(\\mu\\).</p><p>\\(P(Z&gt;\\tfrac{43-\\mu}{5})=0.2119\\Rightarrow\\tfrac{43-\\mu}{5}=0.8\\) (from tables). \\(\\mu=43-4=39\\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "\\(X\\sim N(30,\\sigma^2)\\) and \\(P(X&lt;25)=0.0668\\). Find \\(\\sigma\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(P(Z&lt;\\tfrac{25-30}{\\sigma})=0.0668\\Rightarrow\\tfrac{-5}{\\sigma}=-1.5\\Rightarrow\\sigma=\\tfrac{5}{1.5}\\approx3.33\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
